/*!

*\page i2c_get	I2C Get
*
* This instruction reads data from an I2C device (master or slave). The instruction uses the standard I2C_SCL and I2C_SDA definitions.<BR>
*<span style='color:blue'><em><H4> Syntax: </H4></em></span>
*<B> i2c_get MASTER/SLAVE, address, VARIABLE_receive_data, lengthOfData;</B><BR>
* - <b>MASTER/SLAVE:</b> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;0= Master , 1=Slave
* - <b>ADDRESS:</b>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Address of the MASTER/SLAVE<br>
* - <b>VARIABLE_NAME:</b> You must provide the instruction a variable name. The results will be saved in that variable (might be an array of char). 
* - <b>lengthOfData:</b> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Length of the message or data<br>
*
* <span style='color:blue'><em><B> Example:</B> </em> </span><br>
* myvalue ={245,133};
* i2c_send 1, 1222, myvalue,2;		&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  <span style='color:green'> rem read from the slave 2 bytes</span><br>
*
*
*/
